tion, and the use of preservatives during sample collection</article-title><source>J Proteome Res</source><year>2007</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>4173</fpage><lpage>4181</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17924682</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1021/pr070311+</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Traum</surname><given-names>AZ</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>SELDI-TOF MS of quadruplicate urine and serum samples to evaluate changes related to storage conditions</article-title><source>Proteomics</source><year>2006</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>1676</fpage><lpage>1680</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16447157</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/pmic.200500174</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schaub</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>Urine protein profiling with surface-enhanced laser-desorption/ionization time-of-flight mass spectrometry</article-title><source>Kidney Int</source><year>2004</year><volume>65</volume><fpage>323</fpage><lpage>332</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14675066</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1523-1755.2004.00352.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fiedler</surname><given-names>GM</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>Standardized peptidome profiling of human urine by magnetic bead separation and matrix-assisted laser desorption/ionization time-of-flight mass spectrometry</article-title><source>Clin Chem</source><year>2007</year><volume>53</volume><fpage>421</fpage><lpage>428</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17272489</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1373/clinchem.2006.077834</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-