<surname>Smilde</surname><given-names>AK</given-names></name><name><surname>Werf</surname><given-names>MJ van der</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Centering, scaling, and transformations: improving the biological information content of metabolomics data</article-title><source>BMC Genomics</source><year>2006</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>142</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16762068</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1471-2164-7-142</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schulz-Knappe</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Schrader</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Zucht</surname><given-names>HD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The peptidomics concept, Comb</article-title><source>Chem High Throughput Screen</source><year>2005</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>697</fpage><lpage>704</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2174/138620705774962418</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thongboonkerd</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Chutipongtanate</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kanlaya</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Systematic evaluation of sample preparation methods for gel-based human urinary proteomics: quantity, quality, and variability</article-title><source>J Proteome Res</source><year>2006</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>183</fpage><lpage>191</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16396510</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1021/pr0502525</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>